# Paper-3 experiment scripts that ran here with cwd=cbcd; they belong with the paper, not the library
/experiments/

# FLASH (pds-ball certificate). Dropped as a research direction on 2026-11-16 and deliberately kept
# out of the library: it is an arm to be measured, not part of cbcd. The module stays on disk so the
# untracked time-series local cell can still import it, but it must never ship. The generic local
# cells it was split out of live in cbcd/algorithms/local.py and ARE tracked.
/cbcd/algorithms/_flash.py
_flash*.py

# The i.i.d. local cells from the same research line as FLASH. local_discovery and
# local_discovery_latent implement no published algorithm (the module says "roadmap Phase 3+4"),
# and the Possible-D-Sep adequacy guard they rest on is ours, not a paper's. They stay on disk as
# arms to measure, not as library surface. The published local-latent algorithms live beside them
# in locals_.py and ARE tracked.
/cbcd/algorithms/local.py

# TEMPORARY. The time-series local cell, held back because it still imports the FLASH certificate
# (_finalize_flash_ts + the _flash import) and has not been split the way cbcd/algorithms/local.py
# was. Its three tests under tests/timeseries/ are left visible on purpose, as the reminder that
# this is unfinished rather than abandoned. Remove this line once the file is split.
/cbcd/timeseries/local.py
